This product bundles eight static 3D robot models under
frontend/public/models/, each derived from an upstream ROS description package.
Each .glb ships with a sibling <name>.LICENSE.txt reproducing that upstream's
full licence text, its copyright notice, the exact source commit and mesh paths,
and a modification notice:

  go2.glb               BSD-3-Clause  (C) Unitree Robotics, 2016-2022
  husky.glb             BSD-3-Clause  (C) 2021 Clearpath Robotics Inc.
  jackal.glb            BSD-3-Clause  (C) 2021 Clearpath Robotics Inc.
  limo.glb              BSD-3-Clause  (C) 2021 Agilex Robotics
  rosbot_xl_arm.glb     Apache-2.0    (C) Husarion and the arm's upstream authors
  turtlebot3_burger.glb Apache-2.0    (C) ROBOTIS CO., LTD.
  turtlebot4.glb        Apache-2.0    (C) Clearpath Robotics / turtlebot4_description authors
  waffle_pi.glb         Apache-2.0    (C) ROBOTIS CO., LTD.

BSD-3-Clause requires the copyright notice and licence text to accompany
redistributions; the per-model .LICENSE.txt files satisfy that requirement.
No trademark or endorsement by any of these vendors is implied.
A summary of every third-party component is in THIRD_PARTY.md.

One of those eight, in full detail as a worked example:

  Asset:    frontend/public/models/turtlebot3_burger.glb
  Source:   https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/turtlebot3
  Path:     turtlebot3_description/meshes/{bases/burger_base.stl,
            wheels/{left,right}_tire.stl, sensors/lds.stl}
  License:  Apache License, Version 2.0
  Copyright: ROBOTIS CO., LTD.

  The bundled .glb is a static, non-articulated conversion of those meshes
  (base, two wheels, LiDAR puck assembled per the joint offsets in
  turtlebot3_burger.urdf, decimated, and re-exported). This is a modification
  of the original work as contemplated by Section 4(b) of the Apache License,
  Version 2.0.

  The full license text and modification notice for this asset are
  reproduced in full at:
  frontend/public/models/turtlebot3_burger.LICENSE.txt

  No trademark or endorsement by ROBOTIS is implied.
